Recalbox names the Amiga CD BIOS files kick40060.CD32 / kick40060.CD32.ext and
kick34005.A500 / kick34005.CDTV, and the A600 kickstart kick40063.A600 (see
share_init/.emulationstation/es_bios.xml). None of these were looked up.
The extended ROM names were missing, so -K was never passed and a CD32 booting
on a 512k kickstart never saw a CD. On CDTV, kick34005.CDTV is the extended
ROM, not the kickstart, so kick34005.A500 must be tried first.

